# core/view-diff - What is on one diagram and not the other?
#
# Answers: the set difference between two views, by placed element, with which side
# each element is on. DIRECTION selects a-only, b-only, or symmetric (both
# directions, which is the default).
#
# Does NOT prove: that a difference between diagrams is a difference in the
# architecture. Views are editorial. An element missing from B may have been
# removed, may never have been drawn, or may sit on a third diagram nobody named -
# and an element added to B may be a relabelling of something already in A.
#
# Elements present on BOTH views never appear. That is what a difference is; run
# core/view-contents on either view to see everything it places.
#
# Why this exists as a template: the same question was once answered by running
# core/view-usage over a handful of hand-picked candidate elements. That is
# selection-biased by construction - it can only find what somebody already
# suspected - while this is mechanically complete over both views.
#
# The two sides are scoped INDEPENDENTLY ({{GRAPH_OPEN:views}} and views2, views3,
# views4). Sharing one graph scope would silently require both views to live in the
# same views graph, and comparing a baseline model's view with a target model's view
# - the most valuable case - would then report every element of A as a-only.
#
# REQUIRES the views graph, emitted only where the source carried diagrams.
# Backstage and LeanIX output has none at all, so under a profile where views_graph
# is partial an empty result may mean "this notation has no diagrams" rather than
# "these views are identical".
#
# STR() around ?type is load-bearing: GROUP_CONCAT over IRIs is a type error, and an
# erroring aggregate yields unbound rather than failing, so without it every row
# arrives with an empty types column while the row count still looks right.
#
# Get both view IRIs from core/views rather than constructing them.
#
# Parameters: VIEW_A_IRI, VIEW_B_IRI, DIRECTION, LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT ?side ?element ?label (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT STR(?type); separator=", ") AS ?types) ?nativeId
WHERE {
  {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:views}}
      ?nodeA {{ROLE:view_ref}} {{VIEW_A_IRI}} ;
             {{ROLE:node_element}} ?element .
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      {{GRAPH_OPEN:views2}}
        ?nodeB {{ROLE:view_ref}} {{VIEW_B_IRI}} ;
               {{ROLE:node_element}} ?element .
      {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
    }
    BIND("a-only" AS ?side)
  }
  UNION
  {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:views3}}
      ?nodeB {{ROLE:view_ref}} {{VIEW_B_IRI}} ;
             {{ROLE:node_element}} ?element .
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      {{GRAPH_OPEN:views4}}
        ?nodeA {{ROLE:view_ref}} {{VIEW_A_IRI}} ;
               {{ROLE:node_element}} ?element .
      {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
    }
    BIND("b-only" AS ?side)
  }
  FILTER(?side = {{DIRECTION}} || {{DIRECTION}} = "symmetric")
  OPTIONAL {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
      ?element a ?type .
      OPTIONAL { ?element {{PATH:label}} ?label }
      OPTIONAL { ?element {{PATH:native_id}} ?nativeId }
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
  }
}
GROUP BY ?side ?element ?label ?nativeId
ORDER BY ?side ?label ?element
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
